{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/6525","createdAt":"2026-10-02T06:56:33Z","decision":"accept_intent","decisionDigest":"sha256:5aeaed84f6a0d866eea73c6abc68743ef7f111c9b9555b006696cf91a96f40e1","decisionId":"rdec-c2d375be058b8496b2974059ab03c0a6","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:8231772239b24862f8190f7e5c14d70fbc5420fea97f320a3b4178151012dbd5","packageIdentity":"epkg-d4b93d0ee3933ad0ff5cdcfddc9316d033c36de76bc153d9862602e37eb4168e","prNumber":"6525","reason":"Agree with the intent; one regression to fix first (our GitHub comment, re-checked on this mirror). The inline-comment defect (#13493, KI-MENU-JSONC-INLINE-COMMENT) is fixed, // inside strings survives, trailing commas still parse, and the parse-failure warning is an improvement. Regression, recorded as KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE: a whole-line comment indented with a JS whitespace character JSON does not accept (NBSP, U+2028, U+3000, VT, FF, a byte-order mark after the start) now empties the whole menu file; the old regex removed that character with the comment. Copying any such character outside a string as a plain space keeps the old behaviour. #13968 overlaps on the inline-comment fix. Advisory: we cannot approve for the maintainers.","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/6525","createdAt":"2026-10-02T10:28:22Z","decision":"accept_intent","decisionDigest":"sha256:1930795a64ee50453ddc43a776628e43f66c5fd55b3e8df356c0b3a53d29e3c4","decisionId":"rdec-7153938c86ac6a2863679eae73b62a9e","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:8231772239b24862f8190f7e5c14d70fbc5420fea97f320a3b4178151012dbd5","packageIdentity":"epkg-d4b93d0ee3933ad0ff5cdcfddc9316d033c36de76bc153d9862602e37eb4168e","prNumber":"6525","reason":"Agree with the intent, with one regression to fix first: inline // comments now parse, but a whole-line comment indented with a non-ASCII space now empties the whole menu file. At head 913e112d, a trailing // comment after content parses (1 row, where quattro c05d9019 drops the file), // inside a string survives, trailing commas still parse, and menu-test.sh passes (130 ok). The regression: a no-break space, U+2028, U+3000, a vertical tab or a form feed indenting a // line, or a BOM later in the file, makes the file contribute 0 rows, because JSON.parse accepts only ASCII whitespace. Copying any such character outside a string as a plain space keeps the old behaviour. #13968 fixes the same inline-comment bug (#13493), so whichever lands second needs a rebase.","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
